---
title: Delete a Service
sidebar:
  order: 3
---
Users may need to delete a service listing if it is no longer offered or if they want to keep their service catalog clean and updated. Removing outdated or irrelevant services helps maintain a clear and accurate profile, improving the overall experience for potential clients.

## Pre-conditions to use the Feature

- Users must have a Taskip account
- Users must be logged into that account
- At least one service must exist in the Services section
- Users must have **Super Admin or Admin** permissions to delete a service

## To Delete a Service

### Steps to Use:

**Access Service Management:** Log in to your Taskip account.

**Navigate to Services:** Click on the **Services** section from the main menu.

**Locate Service to Delete:** Identify the service you want to remove. Click the **three-dot (⋮) button** on the right side of the service. A dropdown menu will appear.

**Initiate Deletion:** Click **Delete Service** from the menu.

**Confirmation Prompt:** Taskip will display a confirmation message to ensure you want to proceed with deletion.

**Final Confirmation:** Confirm the action to permanently delete the service. Note that this action is irreversible.

**Service Deletion:** Once confirmed, the service will be permanently removed from your profile and will no longer be visible in the catalog.

Following these steps, users can easily delete services that are no longer relevant or needed in their Taskip account.
